cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this guide or its sample projects in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Edge AI Field Guide: A Beginner-to-Advanced Roadmap for TinyML and On-Device AI"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Prem Chand"
  - name: "awesome-edge-ai contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Premchand006/awesome-edge-ai"
url: "https://premchand006.github.io/awesome-edge-ai/"
abstract: >-
  An 8-phase, beginner-to-advanced curriculum for edge AI and Physical AI:
  foundations, TinyML, efficient model architectures, quantization/pruning/distillation,
  inference runtimes (ONNX Runtime, LiteRT, TensorRT, OpenVINO, RKNN), real-time
  pipelines (GStreamer, DeepStream, ROS 2), edge MLOps, and industry PoCs, with
  verified runnable sample projects.
keywords:
  - edge-ai
  - tinyml
  - on-device-ai
  - quantization
  - onnxruntime
  - tensorrt
  - openvino
  - roadmap
